# Git, Jira, and external systems

- Use protected `main`, governed short-lived branches, registered worktrees, exact
  head checks, and the Repository Steward. Do not push implementation directly to main.
- Use one branch/PR for the cohesive slice, not one per lifecycle state or subtask.
- Jira coordinates work; it does not prove implementation or revise requirements.
- External writes require action identity, exact target, authority, plan/dry-run,
  idempotency, receipt, and readback/reconciliation.
- On an uncertain remote outcome: stop writes, read state, reconcile, and retry only
  when the intended effect is absent and still authorized.
- Keep Cursor cloud implementation workers credential-free. Invoke GitHub/Jira
  mutations only through ProjectPipeline's governed adapters.
